{"id":"word:hebrew:H2583","type":"word","title":"חָנָה","subtitle":"H2583 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"properly, to incline ; by implication, to decline (of the slanting rays of evening); specifically, to pitch a tent; generally to encamp (for abode or siege)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to חָנָה (H2583) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 143 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"חָנָה (chânâh) means properly, to incline ; by implication, to decline (of the slanting rays of evening); specifically, to pitch a tent; generally to encamp (for abode or siege) First listed occurrence: 1Chr 11 15."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"חָנָה","transliteration":"chânâh","pronunciation":"khaw-naw'","strong":"H2583","lemmaId":"hebrew:H2583","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["וַֽ/יַּחֲנ֖וּ","וַֽ/יַּחֲנוּ֙","וַ/יַּחֲנ֣וּ","וַֽ/יַּחֲנ֛וּ","יַחֲנ֖וּ"],"morphs":[["HC/Vqw3mp",80],["HVqi3mp",14],["HC/Vqw3ms",10],["HVqrmpa",5],["HC/Td/Vqrmpa",5],["HTd/Vqrmpa",4],["HVqp3cp",3],["HVqrfsa",2],["HVqp3ms",2],["HVqrmsa",2]]},"definitions":{"short":"properly, to incline ; by implication, to decline (of the slanting rays of evening); specifically, to pitch a tent; generally to encamp (for abode or siege)","usage":"abide (in tents), camp, dwell, encamp, grow to an end, lie, pitch (tent), rest in tent.","full":"H2583. chanah חָנָה 143 verb decline, bend down, encamp (Aramaic to aim at, incline towards, reach ; Zinjirli מחנת construct camp , Inscription Panammu 13. 16. 17 ; Arabic bend, curve, bend down ; Assyrian mûnu, mênu and tênû, couch, mânîtu, house , Zim BP 44, 45 Dl in Zim 117 ) — Qal Perfect חָנָה 1Sam 26:5 ; Isa 29:1 ; וְחָנִ֫יתִי consecutive 29:3 ; Zech 9:8 ; חָנוּ Num 2:34 2 t.; וְחָנוּ consecutive 1:52 ; Imperfect וַיִּחַן Gen 26:17 9 t.; 3 feminine singular תַּחֲנֶה Psa 27:3 ; יַחֲנוּ Num 1:50 13 t. Numbers + Exod 14:2 : וַיַּחֲנוּ Exodus 13:26 79t. (of which 42 in Numbers 33); וַיַּחֲנוּן Judg 11:18 ; 2 masculine plural תַּחֲנוּ Exod 14:2 ; 1 plural וַנַּחֲנֶה Ezra 8:15 ; Imperative חֲנֵה 2Sam 12:28 ; חֲנוּ Num 31:19 ; Jer 50:29 ; Infinitive חֲנוֺת Judg 19:9 ; חֲנֹת Num 1:51 ; suffix חֲנֹתֵנוּ 10:31 ; חֲנֹתְכֶם Deut 1:33 ; Participle חֹנֶה Exod 18:5 ; Psa 34:8 ; feminine חֹנָה 2Sam 23:13 ; 1Chr 11:15 ; חֹנָ֑ךְ Psa 53:6 ; plural חֹנִים Exod 14:9 11 t.; חוֺנִים Num 2:2 ; Nahum 3:17 ; &#8212; 1 decline , of day drawing to its close הַיּוֺם חֲנוֺת Judg 19:9 (|| לַעֲרוֺב הַיּ ׳רָפָה ; also הַיּ ׳נְטוֺת V:8; מְאֹד רַד הַיּוֺם 19:11 ). 2 encamp (properly verge toward, incline to, settle at , of goal of day's march): — a. of single nomad Gen 26:17 (J; followed by ב ), 33:18 (E; followed by אֶתפֿני ). b. of Israel at Exodus and in wilderness Exod 13:20 ( ב ) 14:2 ( לִפְנֵי ), 14:2 ( עַל ), + approximately 80 t. (Hexateuch chiefly P); also (absolute) Num 9:18 , 20 , 22 , 23 compare Ezra 8:15 ; Neh 11:30 so they encamped (i.e. settled , or were settled ) from Beersheba to the valley of Hinnom (|| ישׁבו 11:25 ). c. of armies : (1) Israel (conquering Canaan, etc.) Josh 4:19 ; 5:10 + often; (2) Philistines 1Sam 4:1 ; 13:16 ; 2Sam 23:23 +; usually followed by ב location Num 10:31 ; 1Sam 4:1 ; 13:16 ; Josh 4:19 ; 1Sam 13:5 + 63t. ( בְ וַיַּחֲנוּ 2Sam 24:5 read ᵐ5 מִן וַיָּחֵלּוּ L We Dr see חלל ); so of locusts in hedges (in simile) Nahum 3:17 ; also followed by עַל = by, near Exod 14:2 , 9 ; 15:27 ; Num 1:52 ; 2:2 , 5 , 12 , 27 ; 3:29 , 35 ( ירך על ), 33:10 ; Judg 7:1 ; 1Sam 4:1 ; השׂדה עלפֿני ( על in different sense) 2Sam 11:11 ; followed by עַל also = against, encamp with hostile purpose Josh 10:5 , 31 , 34 ; Judg 6:4 ; 20:19 ; 1Sam 11:1 ; 2Sam 12:28 ; 1Kin 16:15 ; 2Kin 25:1 ; 2Chr 32:1 ; Jer 50:29 ; 52:4 ; Psa 27:3 ; followed by אֶלֿ in same sense Josh 11:5 ; metaphor of God's hostility to apostate Jerusalem ( על ) Isa 29:3 ; followed by also לְ = at, by Num 2:34 ; Zech 9:8 ; אשׁרשָׁ֗֗֗ם Exod 18:5 ; 1Sam 26:5 ; followed by לְ סביב for protection Num 1:50 , 53 , compare metaphor Psa 34:8 , but also hostility Job 19:12 ; also follwed by other prepositions and prepositional phrases, e.g. מֵעֵבֶר Num 21:13 ; מחוץ 31:19 ; בין 1Sam 17:1 ; נגד 1Kin 20:27 etc.; followed by accusative of location 2Sam 17:26 ; followed by suffix accusative with hostile sense חֹנָ֑ךָ Psa 53:6 ; without preposition or noun following, in sense of encamp, be or abide in encampment Num 9:18 , 20 , 22 , 23 ; Ezra 8:15 ; 2Sam 11:11 +; poetic of David in Jerusalem, Isa 29:1 city in which David fixed his camp.","rootNote":"a primitive root (compare 2603 );","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 11 15","keyReferences":["1Chr 11 15","1Chr 19 7","1Kgs 16 15","1Kgs 16 16","1Kgs 20 27","1Kgs 20 29","1Sam 4 1","1Sam 4 1"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":143,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 11 15","book":"1Chr","chapter":11,"verse":15,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"חֹנָ֖ה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqrfsa"},{"reference":"1Chr 19 7","book":"1Chr","chapter":19,"verse":7,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַֽ/יַּחֲנ֖וּ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqw3mp"},{"reference":"1Kgs 16 15","book":"1Kgs","chapter":16,"verse":15,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"חֹנִ֔ים","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqrmpa"},{"reference":"1Kgs 16 16","book":"1Kgs","chapter":16,"verse":16,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/חֹנִ֣ים","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Vqrmpa"},{"reference":"1Kgs 20 27","book":"1Kgs","chapter":20,"verse":27,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יַּחֲנ֨וּ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqw3mp"},{"reference":"1Kgs 20 29","book":"1Kgs","chapter":20,"verse":29,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַֽ/יַּחֲנ֧וּ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqw3mp"},{"reference":"1Sam 4 1","book":"1Sam","chapter":4,"verse":1,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַֽ/יַּחֲנוּ֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqw3mp"},{"reference":"1Sam 4 1","b